# Ship: main + local installs while devving, tags for releases

## While devving (default)

Commit to `master` and push. No tag, no CI release. Then install locally:

- Desktop: `npm run launch:mac` / local `package:*` on the dev machine.
- Mobile: `npm run mobile:release` (pins `../HANDCASH-MOBILE` to this commit, bumps and tags it locally), push Mobile master + its `v0.1.x` tag, install the APK its `release-apk.yml` signs and publishes, `npm run mobile:check`. A local `build-apk.sh` has no release key, so its APK cannot upgrade a phone's install.

`scripts/require-version-bump.mjs` and `.githooks/pre-push` enforce `package.json` version > latest remote `v*` tag, so bump `package.json` + `src/version.ts` + `docs/releases/X.Y.Z.md` on each push.

## Public release (only when the user names one)

```bash
git push origin master
git tag vX.Y.Z
git push origin vX.Y.Z
```

Workflows on `v*` tags: `release-mac.yml`, `release-windows.yml`, `release-linux.yml`. Do not wait on local `package:*` for a release.

Desktop no longer dispatches Mobile. A `v0.1.x` tag pushed in `HANDCASH-MOBILE` runs its `release-apk.yml`, which signs and publishes the APK + `.sha256` (not a draft).
